<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nathan (prophet)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nathan was a prophet at the court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/david">King David</a> according to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hebrew-bible">Hebrew Bible</a>. He conveyed God's promise of an enduring dynasty to David, rebuked him with a parable for his adultery with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bathsheba">Bathsheba</a> and the killing of Uriah, and, with Bathsheba, secured the succession of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/solomon">Solomon</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/adonijah">Adonijah</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nathan-prophet.jpg" alt="Nathan (prophet)" width="320" height="370" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Palma il Giovane · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Jacopo_Negretti,_gen._Palma_il_Giovane_und_Werkstatt_-_Prophet_Nathan_ermahnt_K%C3%B6nig_David_-_GG_3816_-_Kunsthistorisches_Museum.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
